article_content:
The 16-piece limited-edition collection features clean silhouettes and elevated wardrobe staples in line with Victoria Beckham ’s signature minimalist aesthetic. Products include lace-trimmed satin-crepe gowns in white and black colourways, a camel-hued suede shirt, trousers and midi skirt, alongside matching tote and shoulder bags. The partnership builds on Net-a-Porter ’s continued focus on exclusivity and curated luxury, following similar collaborations with brands such as Loewe, Loro Piana and Tod’s. Retail prices range from £590 for a lace-trimmed satin-crepe camisole top to £1,990 for a lace-trimmed crepe and satin-crepe gown. #gallery-1 {
                margin: auto;
            }
            #gallery-1 .gallery-item {
                float: left;
                margin-top: 10px;
                text-align: center;
                width: 33%;           }
            #gallery-1 img {
                border: 2px solid #cfcfcf;
            }
            #gallery-1 .gallery-caption {
                margin-left: 0;
            } Victoria Beckham saw total revenues climb 26% to £112.7m in the year to 31 December 2024 , marking the fourth consecutive year of double-digit revenue growth for the former Spice Girl’s eponymous brand. For SS24, the brand collaborated with Spanish high street retailer Mango on a capsule collection featuring tailoring, lingerie dresses, knitwear and accessories.
